A)
, substitution
B)
, insertion
C)
, and deletion
D)
rates were summed and separately plotted for 5′ untranslated region (5′UTR), coding sequence (CDS), and 3′ untranslated region (3′UTR); genotypes and temperature regimes are displayed under diagrams. Bars represent standard errors,
n
≥ 3;
P
-values based on 2-tailed Student's
t
-test (
⋕
P
< 0.05,
⋕⋕
P
< 0.01,
⋕⋕⋕
P
< 0.001) for CDS vs 5′ or 3′UTR comparisons are shown only.
Transcripts with nucleotide insertions in CDS are destabilised by the NMD pathway
TFIIS genetically interacts with the NMD pathway
If both TFIIS and NMD contribute to the reduction of downstream negative effects of faulty transcription, then the TFIIS and NMD mutants should genetically interact. To analyze the interaction between the TFIIS and NMD pathways, we studied the development and HS-sensitivity of
upf1-5
and
upf3-1
single, and
tfIIs;upf1
and
tfIIs;upf3
double mutant plants (
Fig. 4
). Under normal temperature, the
tfIIs-1
shows essentially a wild-type phenotype (
Grasser et al. 2009
), while the
upf1-5
plants have minor developmental defects, including jagged and slightly narrow leaves (
Arciga-Reyes et al. 2006
). The
upf3-1
displays stronger developmental alterations, with well-marked rosette leaf shape and floral morphological changes, and slightly retarded growth compared to wild type (
Arciga-Reyes et al. 2006
) (
Fig. 4A
). The developmental phenotype of the
nmd
single mutants became severely intensified in the double mutant combinations; the
tfIIs;upf1
plants formed narrow, downward curling leaves with wavy and serrated edges but seeded normally. The
tfIIs;upf3
plants showed dramatic growth phenotype, they were stunted and failed to flower at normal temperature (LD, 21 °C). Their leaf shape alterations were similar as in the
tfIIs;upf1
, but more extreme, the overall rosette growth was strongly retarded. Flowering was slightly accelerated in
tfIIs-1
(
Grasser et al. 2009
) but was delayed in
upf1-5, tfIIs;upf1
and
upf3-1
compared to Col-0. The
tfIIs;upf3
mutant flowered only at higher temperature (LD, 25 °C), and its flowering was still significantly retarded (
Supplementary Fig. S10A
).
Figure 4.
NMD pathway is needed for heat stress survival.
A)
Phenotype of
tfIIs-1, upf1-5, upf3-1, tfIIs-1;upf1-5, and tfIIs-1;upf3-1
mutants vs wt (Col-0) at ambient growth conditions (LD, 21 °C);
B)
Box plot of the NMD target transcripts (fragments per kilobase per million, FPKM; box plot elements: center line, median; box limits second and third quartiles; whiskers, upper and lower quartiles), conditions and genotypes are shown;
n
= 3, statistical difference (mutants vs Col-0 (wt))
P
-values based on 2-tailed Student's
t
-test, ***
P
< 0.001;
C)
Heat-sensitivity phenotype of
upf1-5
and
upf3-1
mutants compared to Col-0 (wt); treatment durations are indicated, and
quantification of TMHT experiments are shown in
Supplementary Fig. S15A
;
D)
Schematic of heat stress regime, thermotolerance to moderately high temperature (TMHT) and non-treated (NT) control, and triangles denote picturing times.
RNA quality control pathway NMD supports development and adaptation to high temperatures.
We have also conducted an automated phenotyping examination on the mutant series (
Supplementary Fig. S10, B to G
). The morphological data measured by RGB sensors showed that the
tfIIs-1, tfIIs;upf1
, and especially the
tfIIs;upf3
mutants are smaller compared to Col-0,
upf1-5
, and
upf3-1,
respectively. While the genotypes Col-0,
upf1-5, upf3-1,
and
tfIIs;upf1
retained their round shape, the mutant plants
tfIIs-1
and
tfIIs;upf3
were oval shaped, as presented by higher eccentricity values. The TCARI (Transformed Chlorophyll Absorption Reflectance Index) values, related to the chlorophyll content of leaves showed a similar tendency, and were lower in
tfIIs-1, tfIIs;upf1,
and
tfIIs;upf3
mutants compared to Col-0,
upf1-5,
or
upf3-1
(
Supplementary Fig. S10E
). This trait was also manifested in the color segmentation data (
Supplementary Fig. S10G
). TFIIS mutation impact on leaf pigment content was limited, since the
F
v
/
F
m
chlorophyll fluorescence parameter (representing the optimal quantum efficiency of PSII) remained unchanged, except for
tfIIs;upf3
mutants, where it dropped significantly (
Supplementary Fig. S10F
).
The typical stunted growth in the NMD mutants is the result of an autoimmune response caused by the stabilization of PTC-containing immune receptor mRNAs (
Gloggnitzer et al. 2014
). To understand the basis of developmental phenotype alterations of the
tfIIs;upf
mutants, we measured the
PATHOGENESIS RELATED GENE 1
(
PR1
) mRNA levels, a marker gene of immunity (
Gloggnitzer et al. 2014
). In wild-type Col-0,
tfIIs-1, upf1-5
single, and
tfIIs;upf1
double mutants, the level of
PR1
mRNA was very low, while in
upf3-1
was slightly elevated at 21 °C, ∼5-fold vs Col-0, suggesting a mild autoimmune status of this line (
Supplementary Fig. S11A
). Notably,
PR1
increased dramatically in
tfIIs;upf3
(∼500-fold vs Col-0), showing that the absence of TFIIS causes intensification of the immunity response in the strong NMD mutant background
upf3-1
, but not in
upf1-5
, in correlation with their phenotypes. These observations were also confirmed by RNA transcriptome; several immune response genes were overexpressed in the
tfIIs;upf3
mutants at normal temperature (
see later
).
High ambient temperature suppresses the autoimmune response of NMD mutants (
Gloggnitzer et al. 2014
). Therefore, we measured
PR1
changes at 25 °C and 28 °C.
PR1
accumulation decreased to background level in
tfIIs;upf3
plants were already at 25 °C (
Supplementary Fig. S11A
). Besides, we also examined the developmental changes at 25 °C: the stunted growth phenotype of
tfIIs;upf3
plants was partially suppressed (
Supplementary Fig. S11B
), in correlation with the reduction in
PR1
mRNA levels. Despite the still strong growth phenotypes at 25 °C,
tfIIs;upf3
were able to proceed into the generative phase and produce very few seeds. Notably, the leaf shape alterations of
tfIIs;upf3
were constant at both 21 °C and 25 °C temperature and were very similar to
tfIIs;upf1
leaf shape phenotype, suggesting that the NMD deficiency-caused leaf/rosette phenotype is independent of the autoimmunity.
NMD is needed for efficient HS response
In plants, biotic and abiotic stresses can modify NMD activity, but the roles of NMD in HS adaptation were not analyzed before (
Shi et al. 2012
;
Kurosaki et al. 2019
;
Luha et al. 2024
). To test if NMD maintains its activity during elevated heat, we measured the level of selected NMD targets in plants under control conditions or exposed to short-term (TMHT/1h) or persistent HS (TMHT/1d) and following two-day recovery period (RE) (see Materials and Methods).
eRF1-1
(
Nyiko et al. 2017
) and
SMG7
(
Nyiko et al. 2013
) are NMD-regulated transcripts bearing NMD-inducing introns in their 3′UTR, while
At3g53400
and
At5g45430
are NMD targets possessing uORFs (
Degtiar et al. 2015
). All tested NMD targets were maintained at low level in Col-0 and
tfIIs-1
(∼2-6-fold lower vs
upf1-5
or
upf3-1
background plants) suggesting that they are efficiently destabilized by NMD under ambient conditions (
Supplementary Fig. S12
). Moreover, in the NMD-functional lines (Col-0 and
tfIIs-1
), all these NMD targets remained at a low level throughout all heat treatments (∼3-6-fold lower vs
upf1-5
or
upf3-1
plants), showing that NMD functions during HS. The TFIIS and NMD factors (UPF1, UPF3) do not regulate each other at the transcriptional level during ambient or HS conditions (
Supplementary Fig. S13
), except that
UPF3
mRNA was increased in
tfIIs-1
background at TMHT/1d, implying a TFIIS-UPF3 regulatory loop.
TFIIS
mRNA HS-changes in Col-0 and
tfIIs-1
confirmed previous findings (
Szadeczky-Kardoss et al. 2022
).
To analyze NMD functionality genome-wide, we performed an RNA transcriptome analysis (see Materials and Methods). To strictly select the potential NMD direct targets (referred to as NMD targets), we considered the differentially expressed genes (DEGs) that were upregulated significantly (
P
< 0.01) and at least 1.4-fold in both
upf1-5
and
upf3-1
NMD mutants compared to Col-0 at NT condition (
n
= 304). Relevantly, the NMD targets were overexpressed in the
nmd
single and double mutants relative to the NMD-functional plants (e.g. Col-0 and
